# Runtime state, not source. `upgrade.ps1` writes state.json as its resume
# journal; committing it would make a fresh machine think steps already ran.
state.json
state.rolled-back-*.json

# Raw `prisma migrate diff` output. It is the drafting input for
# bridge-00-enums.sql / bridge-10-additive.sql / bridge-30-contract.sql, which
# ARE committed. Keeping the draft out avoids ambiguity about which file is
# authoritative. (This kit writes the draft to C:\POS-BACKUPS\work\ anyway.)
draft.sql
bridge-draft.sql

# Fingerprints and preflight JSON are machine- and run-specific; the reports
# that matter are summarised in REHEARSAL-1-REPORT.md.
fingerprint-report.json
*-before.json

# MigrationReport.{json,md} are deliberately NOT ignored - they are the
# deployment evidence for what the account mapping did, and belong in history.
